    "result_text": "Done. The change is implemented and the full test suite is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nI added a `checkDigit` field to the owner returned by the API, defined as a single Luhn check digit computed over the digits of the `customerCode`.\n\nSince `checkDigit` is a purely derived value (like `initials`, `membershipLevel`, `locality`, `identityKey`), I implemented it as a mapper-computed field rather than a stored column \u2014 consistent with the existing pattern in this codebase:\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added a `checkDigit` property to the `Owner` schema (integer 0\u20139, `readOnly`), which the OpenAPI generator turns into the DTO field `OwnerDto.checkDigit`.\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 Added a `@Mapping(target = \"checkDigit\", ...)` binding plus a `checkDigit(owner)` method and a `luhn(String)` helper. The Luhn algorithm mirrors the one the acceptance test uses (right-to-left, doubling every second digit starting from the rightmost, digits >9 reduced by 9, result making the sum a multiple of ten). It returns `null` when no `customerCode` is present.\n\nBecause `customerCode` is persisted on create, the mapper recomputes `checkDigit` correctly on any `GET /api/owners/{id}`.\n\n**Tests:** `AcceptanceTest.coreCheckDigitIsLuhnOfCustomerCode` passes, and the full suite is green (`BUILD SUCCESS`, `Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0`).",
